<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span>Example state-only prompts for the IPD, IMP, ICG and ISH. The structure remains the same across games, with the only differences being the action labels and reward matrices. The specific examples shown are for rounds in which the previous joint action is <math id="A1.F14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{1},a_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{1},a_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
