<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span>Example state-occurrence prompts for the IPD, IMP, ICG and ISH. The structure remains the same across games, with the only differences being the action labels and reward matrices. The specific examples shown are for rounds in which all previous joint actions within the game are <math id="A1.F15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{2},a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{2},a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, except the last one, which is <math id="A1.F15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{1},a_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{1},a_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
